# Trivy vulnerability ignores.
#
# All entries below are transitive dependencies of Astro 5.x reaching the
# `apps/frontend` lockfile. They are *build-time* tools (Vite, picomatch,
# defu) — not part of the deployed runtime, which is a static SSR build
# served by Deno. Real-world exposure is low:
#   - vite WebSocket bypass: dev-server only; production output is static
#   - picomatch ReDoS: requires attacker-controlled glob patterns
#   - defu prototype pollution: invoked internally by build tools only
#
# Patched versions exist but Astro hasn't bumped to them yet, and forcing
# them via `overrides` breaks the build (CommonJS resolver mismatch).
#
# Revisit when:
#   - Astro upgrades these transitives, OR
#   - We migrate the frontend off Deno to npm (see project memory) and
#     can manage the dep tree directly.
#
# Re-evaluate by 2026-08-05 (90 days).

CVE-2026-35209 exp:2026-08-05  # defu: prototype pollution
CVE-2026-33671 exp:2026-08-05  # picomatch: ReDoS via crafted extglob
CVE-2026-39363 exp:2026-08-05  # vite: dev-server WebSocket info disclosure
